# Wrapper scopes for `Section1`

> Module Section1Wrappers

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using SaraStatus as St
> Using Section7703 as S7703
> Using Section152 as S152
> Using Section63 as S63
> Using Section1 as Src

Generated by `cutecat_scripts/generate_dataset.py`; edits are
overwritten. Each scope below adds no rule: it declares one input
per parameter of a top-level function of the port and returns what
that function returns. CUTECat explores one entry point per run,
and a top-level function is not one until something names it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FnBracketsOf:
  input sched content Src.Schedule
  output result content list of Src.Bracket

declaration scope FnBracketTax:
  input b content Src.Bracket
  input taxable_income content money
  output result content money

declaration scope FnBracketApplies:
  input b content Src.Bracket
  input taxable_income content money
  output result content boolean

declaration scope FnScheduleOf:
  input st content St.Status
  output result content Src.Schedule

```

```catala
scope FnBracketsOf:
  definition result equals Src.brackets_of of sched

scope FnBracketTax:
  definition result equals Src.bracket_tax of b, taxable_income

scope FnBracketApplies:
  definition result equals Src.bracket_applies of b, taxable_income

scope FnScheduleOf:
  definition result equals Src.schedule_of of st

```
